1
00:00:02,540 --> 00:00:03,740
空间
Space.

2
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:06,670
看起来会永远存在
It seems like it must go on forever.

3
00:00:08,190 --> 00:00:09,530
但确实是吗？
But does it?

4
00:00:09,640 --> 00:00:12,560
在宇宙的最深处
Out there in the farthest depths of the Universe,

5
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:14,500
是否有某种地方
might there be someplace

6
00:00:14,610 --> 00:00:18,120
事物归于虚无
where something turns into absolutely nothing?

7
00:00:21,090 --> 00:00:24,640
科学家观测宇宙的最深处
Scientists are probing the far-flung reaches of the cosmos,

8
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:27,150
试图通过探测外部的界限
trying to detect that outer limit,

9
00:00:27,260 --> 00:00:30,330
去发现宇宙的形状
to find the shape of space.

10
00:00:35,830 --> 00:00:38,960
现在令人惊讶的证据被提出
Now surprising evidence suggests

11
00:00:39,070 --> 00:00:42,160
不单只我们的宇宙，是否会在某一个地方有尽头
that not only is there a place where the Universe ends,

12
00:00:42,270 --> 00:00:45,330
而是有别的什么东西潜伏在外面
but that there might be something lurking beyond it --

13
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:49,950
一些难以想象的陌生事物
something unimaginably alien.

14
00:00:52,830 --> 00:00:55,840
科学频道 - 穿越虫洞 2x02
Science.Channel - Through the Wormhole 2x02

15
00:00:56,220 --> 00:01:01,060
空间，时间，生命
Space,time,life itself.

16
00:01:03,190 --> 00:01:07,720
宇宙的秘密，尽在穿越虫洞
The secrets of the cosmos lie through the wormhole.

17
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:18,400
宇宙真的有边缘吗？
Is There an Edge to the Universe?

18
00:01:19,670 --> 00:01:24,390
有时，会有一个很大的观点被提出
Once in a while,a really big idea comes along --

19
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:28,730
它会改变我们对自身的想法
one that completely changes our concept of who we are.

20
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:32,770
1543年，Nicolas Copernicus证明地球
In 1543,Nicolas Copernicus proved that the Earth

21
00:01:32,880 --> 00:01:36,200
并不是宇宙的中心
was not at the center of the cosmos.

22
00:01:36,320 --> 00:01:39,000
1920年代，Edwin Hubble看见
In the 1920s,Edwin Hubble saw

23
00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:41,040
所有宇宙中的星系
that all the galaxies in the Universe

24
00:01:41,150 --> 00:01:43,610
正在加速远离
were rushing away from one another,

25
00:01:43,720 --> 00:01:45,680
让人意识到
sparking the idea

26
00:01:45,790 --> 00:01:48,850
宇宙并不是永远不变的
that the Universe had not been here forever

27
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:52,350
而是创始于一个爆炸性的时刻
but was created in one explosive moment --

28
00:01:52,460 --> 00:01:54,150
宇宙大爆炸
the Big Bang.

29
00:01:54,270 --> 00:01:58,760
现在，我们面对一个里程碑式的改变
Now another monumental change is upon us.

30
00:01:58,870 --> 00:02:03,660
我们长久以来想象宇宙是无限大的
We've long imagined the Universe to be infinite in size,

31
00:02:03,780 --> 00:02:08,270
但现在很多宇宙学家认为，宇宙是…
but many cosmologists now think the Universe...

32
00:02:08,380 --> 00:02:09,800
有限的
is finite.

33
00:02:09,920 --> 00:02:13,970
其中一些人相信，他们知道宇宙的形状
Some believe they even know its shape.

34
00:02:14,090 --> 00:02:16,840
如果我们确实发现了宇宙的边缘
If we do discover an edge to the Universe,

35
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:18,440
我们必须面对
we'll have to grapple

36
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:22,720
另外一个非常有挑战性的，令人不安的问题
with another very challenging and unsettling question.

37
00:02:22,830 --> 00:02:26,160
边缘之外有什么？
What lies beyond the edge?

38
00:02:28,630 --> 00:02:31,190
每天，我在回家的路上
Every day on my way home from school,

39
00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:33,890
我都会经过一面很长的墙
I used to pass a long wall.

40
00:02:34,010 --> 00:02:38,230
它至少是我身高的两倍
It was at least twice my height.

41
00:02:38,340 --> 00:02:40,830
我没有机会看过去
I had no change of seeing over it,

42
00:02:40,950 --> 00:02:44,840
但我能听到背后的声音
but I could hear strange sounds coming from behind it.

43
00:02:44,950 --> 00:02:47,770
我的思想变得狂野
My mind ran wild

44
00:02:47,780 --> 00:02:52,500
想象着会有什么东西在后面呢
imagining what might be back there.

45
00:02:52,510 --> 00:02:54,750
猛兽？悍匪？
Wild animals? Outlaws?

46
00:02:54,760 --> 00:02:58,620
或令人恐惧的怪兽？
Or some fearsome monster?

47
00:02:58,730 --> 00:03:01,090
我会用一只耳朵靠着墙
I would press my ear up against it

48
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:04,020
试图辨认那是什么
to try and decipher what it could be.

49
00:03:04,140 --> 00:03:08,710
我从来没有发现，但我从来不会停止我的好奇心
I never did find out,but I never stopped wondering.

50
00:03:11,040 --> 00:03:14,800
Neil Cornish是个宇宙学家
Neil Cornish is a cosmologist

51
00:03:14,910 --> 00:03:19,740
他生活在蒙大拿，一个有着广阔天空的国家
who lives and works in the big sky country of Montana.

52
00:03:19,850 --> 00:03:21,640
这里唯一的墙
The only walls out here

53
00:03:21,750 --> 00:03:25,510
是一个防止马匹跑出去的篱笆
are fences to keep his horses from roaming off.

54
00:03:25,620 --> 00:03:28,580
从很多同行当中，Neil是最近开始
Neil is the latest in a long line of thinkers

55
00:03:28,690 --> 00:03:31,550
仔细揣摩宇宙大小的
to contemplate the size of the Universe.

56
00:03:31,660 --> 00:03:35,190
首先我们知道的，是希腊的哲学之王
The first we know of was a Greek philosopher king

57
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:38,090
名字叫Architus
called Architus.

58
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:39,660
这个希腊哲学家
The Greek philosopher Architus

59
00:03:39,770 --> 00:03:42,660
对于为何宇宙是无限的，有一个论证
offered an argument for why the Universe must be infinite.

60
00:03:42,770 --> 00:03:45,760
他说，"如果我们来到宇宙的边缘
He said,"if I was to go out to the edge of the Universe

61
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:48,300
我让我的同僚站在这儿
"and then extend my staff to here,

62
00:03:48,410 --> 00:03:51,070
这儿就是宇宙的边缘了"
"that would now be the edge of the Universe.

63
00:03:51,180 --> 00:03:53,640
"然后，如果我让我的同僚站在这儿
"And then,if I was to extend my staff to here,

64
00:03:53,750 --> 00:03:56,440
这儿就变成新的宇宙边缘了"
"that would now be the new edge of the Universe.

65
00:03:56,560 --> 00:03:58,940
"然后，如果我让我的同僚站在那边
"And if I was to extend my staff out to here,

66
00:03:59,060 --> 00:04:01,410
那边又是宇宙的边缘了"
"that would now be the edge of the Universe.

67
00:04:01,530 --> 00:04:04,220
"所以，宇宙必须是无边的。"
So the Universe must be infinite."

68
00:04:04,330 --> 00:04:07,550
Architus's的智力游戏定下的基调
Architus's mental game set the tone

69
00:04:07,670 --> 00:04:10,690
是2千年来科学家的教条
for over 2,000 years of scientific dogma --

70
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:13,990
我们的宇宙必须是无限大的
our Universe must be infinitely large

71
00:04:14,110 --> 00:04:16,060
而且存在永远
and has existed forever.

72
00:04:16,170 --> 00:04:20,000
但现在这教条被改变了
But that dogma is now being challenged.

73
00:04:20,110 --> 00:04:22,430
但是，宇宙无限说存在一个问题
So,one problem with an infinite universe

74
00:04:22,550 --> 00:04:24,470
不止空间无限
that's not just infinite in space

75
00:04:24,580 --> 00:04:27,240
而且时间也是无限，无始无终
but also infinite in time -- has no beginning --

76
00:04:27,350 --> 00:04:29,270
你会有无限的星体
you have an infinite number of stars.

77
00:04:29,390 --> 00:04:32,340
所以，天空会全部是明亮的
So the sky would be just completely covered in white,

78
00:04:32,460 --> 00:04:35,880
亮，更亮，所以星光会把你烤成烧猪
bright,bright -- so bright that it would fry you.

79
00:04:35,990 --> 00:04:38,420
所以，这并不是我们在晚上看到的
So,when we look out at night,that's not what we see.

80
00:04:38,530 --> 00:04:39,750
我们看见星星在这儿，那儿
We see a star here or there

81
00:04:39,870 --> 00:04:41,850
本质上，黑暗也无处不在
and then,essentially,darkness all around.

82
00:04:41,970 --> 00:04:43,320
所以，我们会发现
So this tells us something.

83
00:04:43,440 --> 00:04:46,030
我们并非在一个无限的宇宙中生活
It tells us we don't live in an infinite Universe

84
00:04:46,140 --> 00:04:47,260
那个无限老旧的
that's infinitely old.

85
00:04:47,370 --> 00:04:49,660
是我们黑暗的天空
It was our dark sky

86
00:04:49,780 --> 00:04:53,100
这启发了一个关于宇宙的革命性的想法
that inspired a revolutionary idea about the cosmos --

87
00:04:53,210 --> 00:04:56,500
那就是它不可能永远在这儿
that it cannot have been here forever.

88
00:04:56,620 --> 00:04:59,770
宇宙大爆炸
The Big Bang --

89
00:04:59,890 --> 00:05:03,540
是我们能看见所有空间和物质的一刻
a moment where all the space and matter we can see

90
00:05:03,660 --> 00:05:05,810
从无到有
burst into existence,

91
00:05:05,920 --> 00:05:08,860
从一点扩张开来
expanding out from a single point.

92
00:05:11,060 --> 00:05:12,920
但大爆炸理论，对于天文学家探索宇宙的边缘
But the Big Bang creates a problem

93
00:05:13,030 --> 00:05:15,850
又衍生出一个问题
for astronomers searching for the edge of the Universe.

94
00:05:15,970 --> 00:05:18,290
因为光需要时间
Because it takes light time

95
00:05:18,400 --> 00:05:20,690
去穿越极大的空间
to travel across the vastness of space,

96
00:05:20,810 --> 00:05:23,560
宇航员总是看到过去发生的
astronomers were always looking back in time,

97
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:27,430
直到他们没有时间了
and,eventually,they run out of time.

98
00:05:27,550 --> 00:05:29,600
所以，当我们在晚上看星星的时候
So,when we look out at the stars at night,

99
00:05:29,710 --> 00:05:32,840
我们看到的是多年前的星星
we're seeing those stars as they were years ago.

100
00:05:32,950 --> 00:05:35,010
临近的星体，可能是几年前的
The nearby stars,maybe a few years ago.

101
00:05:35,120 --> 00:05:37,580
星系间的，就是几千年前的了
Looking out across the galaxy,thousands of years ago.

102
00:05:37,690 --> 00:05:39,010
而一直追溯回去
And going back and back,

103
00:05:39,120 --> 00:05:42,380
我们看到的星系，几十亿年前
we see galaxies back billions of years ago.

104
00:05:42,490 --> 00:05:45,080
然后，我们再也看不到
And then,beyond that,where we see no more galaxies.

105
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:46,690
130亿年前的星系
13 billion years ago

106
00:05:46,800 --> 00:05:49,150
那就是我们接着需要解构的了
is the next thing that we've managed to image,

107
00:05:49,270 --> 00:05:52,960
那就是大爆炸的余晖
and it is the after-glow of the Big Bang.

108
00:05:53,070 --> 00:05:56,300
宇宙背景微波辐射
It's called the cosmic microwave background,

109
00:05:56,410 --> 00:05:59,160
它描述了一副宇宙外观的图
and it's a picture of the way the Universe looked

110
00:05:59,280 --> 00:06:02,840
大爆炸后400,000年
about 400,000 years after the Big Bang.

111
00:06:02,950 --> 00:06:06,000
宇宙充满着炽热的气体，等离子体
The Universe is filled with this hot gas,this hot plasma.

112
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:08,310
光线其实不能进发出来
Light really can't go anywhere.

113
00:06:08,420 --> 00:06:10,710
所以，我们不能再往回看了
So we can't see any further back,

114
00:06:10,820 --> 00:06:13,180
就像我们不能看到太阳内部
just as we can't see into the Sun.

115
00:06:13,290 --> 00:06:16,680
宇宙微波背景辐射
The cosmic microwave background

116
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:19,520
就像一个屏障
is a barrier that blocks our vision.

117
00:06:19,630 --> 00:06:22,960
在那后面，可能有一个边缘
Behind it,there could be an edge.

118
00:06:23,070 --> 00:06:26,630
或者，宇宙并不是永远延伸
Or perhaps the Universe does extend on forever.

119
00:06:26,740 --> 00:06:30,260
但无论我们的望远镜多么强大
But no matter how powerful our telescopes become,

120
00:06:30,380 --> 00:06:34,580
我们永远看不到那个领域
that domain will never be visible.

121
00:06:39,150 --> 00:06:41,170
但或许我们有其他方法去探索
But there might be another way to discover

122
00:06:41,290 --> 00:06:43,740
是否我们的宇宙有一个边缘
if the Universe has an edge.

123
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:45,580
Janna Levin是个理论家
Janna Levin is a theoretician

124
00:06:45,690 --> 00:06:48,810
他用复杂的数据模型
who uses complex numerical simulations

125
00:06:48,930 --> 00:06:53,360
去解决科学中最具挑战的问题
to solve some of science's most challenging problems.

126
00:06:57,100 --> 00:06:59,490
你可能会感到惊讶，一个叫 小行星 的老游戏
It might surprise you that a game as old as "Asteroids"

127
00:06:59,600 --> 00:07:01,460
或许能告诉我们关于宇宙的一些东西
can teach us something about the Universe,

128
00:07:01,570 --> 00:07:03,330
必须有一些游戏规则
but there's a rule in the game

129
00:07:03,440 --> 00:07:05,760
令游戏之外的世界感觉靠谱
to make a world out of the game that makes sense,

130
00:07:05,880 --> 00:07:08,770
如果你超过了顶部，你可以从底部重新进来
where,if you exit the top,you re-enter the bottom,

131
00:07:08,880 --> 00:07:11,740
如果你超过了左边，你从右边回来
or if you exit the left,you re-enter from the right.

132
00:07:11,850 --> 00:07:13,570
那些规则创造了
And that rule makes this world

133
00:07:13,690 --> 00:07:15,770
这个游戏的世界
in which you're playing the game,

134
00:07:15,890 --> 00:07:17,580
你玩的这个游戏里的空间
this space in which you're playing the game,

135
00:07:17,690 --> 00:07:19,240
是有限的
a finite space.

136
00:07:19,360 --> 00:07:20,480
那有点像
And that's kind of like

137
00:07:20,590 --> 00:07:22,310
我们想象的宇宙规则
the rules we're imagining for the Universe.

138
00:07:22,430 --> 00:07:25,180
如果我们的宇宙是有限的
If our Universe is finite,

139
00:07:25,300 --> 00:07:28,990
科学家相信它的边缘是有联系的
scientists believe its edges must also be linked,

140
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:30,860
那就是整个宇宙
that the entire cosmos

141
00:07:30,970 --> 00:07:34,430
有点像一个巨大的 小行星 游戏
must act like a giant game of "Asteroids."

142
00:07:34,540 --> 00:07:37,860
如果我们能弯曲这个空间
If we could bend this space,

143
00:07:37,980 --> 00:07:40,800
我们能更直观的看到
we would see that it looks like something more intuitive.

144
00:07:40,910 --> 00:07:43,400
比如，如果我拿起这个菜单
Like,for example,if I were to take this menu

145
00:07:43,520 --> 00:07:45,540
然后应用 小行星 里面的规则
and apply that rule from the "Asteroid" game.

146
00:07:45,650 --> 00:07:47,640
你知道，我跳出顶部，我从底部进入
You know,I exit the top,I enter the bottom.

147
00:07:47,750 --> 00:07:50,140
那其实就像游戏里一样，把菜单
That's exactly the same as taking the menu

148
00:07:50,260 --> 00:07:53,180
卷起，把两头沾在一起
and rolling it up and gluing the sides together.

149
00:07:53,290 --> 00:07:54,910
效果是一样的
It gives the same effect.

150
00:07:55,030 --> 00:07:58,750
如果我能弯曲这个有点硬的菜单
And if I could bend this rather too stiff menu,

151
00:07:58,860 --> 00:08:00,250
我会尝试去弯曲它
I would try to bend it

152
00:08:00,370 --> 00:08:03,620
这两个边缘会沾在一起
so that the two edges came together and were glued.

153
00:08:03,740 --> 00:08:05,760
然后我就做出了一个有点像
And then I'd be making something kind of like,

154
00:08:05,870 --> 00:08:08,290
你知道，一个经典的纽约硬面包圈
you know,a bagel -- a classic,New York bagel.

155
00:08:08,410 --> 00:08:11,730
面包圈是沾在一起的，不只是像个圆柱体
And the bagel is glued together not just like a cylinder

156
00:08:11,840 --> 00:08:13,630
而是两边连在一起
but also around the other side.

157
00:08:13,750 --> 00:08:18,300
虽然面包圈表面明显是有限的
Even though the surface of this bagel is clearly finite,

158
00:08:18,420 --> 00:08:21,770
但没有人能在里面找到边缘
no one living in this space would ever run into an edge,

159
00:08:21,890 --> 00:08:24,780
所以感觉就像它是无边际，无限的
so it feels boundless and infinite.

160
00:08:24,890 --> 00:08:26,610
当我们生活在这个宇宙
When we live inside the Universe,

161
00:08:26,730 --> 00:08:28,480
我们不能走出去
we can't step outside of it.

162
00:08:28,590 --> 00:08:30,880
因为这儿没有其他维度往下
There's no other dimension to look down from,

163
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:34,550
看着我们的3维空间的宇宙，所以那很难被观察到
onto our 3-dimensional Universe,so it's harder to visualize.

164
00:08:34,670 --> 00:08:36,290
但我们可以利用规则
But we can use the rules

165
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:39,790
就像用在 小行星 游戏里的规则
like the rules that are used in the "Asteroids" game.

166
00:08:39,900 --> 00:08:41,630
然后我们加上一条
And then we add one more rule

167
00:08:41,740 --> 00:08:43,560
3个规则，3个维度
for three rules for three dimensions.

168
00:08:43,680 --> 00:08:47,500
从后面进去，从前面出来
Go out the back face,come in the front.

169
00:08:47,610 --> 00:08:50,600
如果我们生活在一个宇宙立方体里面
If we do live in a cosmic asteroid cube,

170
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:53,740
这里有个方法我们可以探索宇宙的边界
there is a way we could discover the edges --

171
00:08:53,850 --> 00:08:56,010
不是用飞船飞越它
not by flying a spaceship across them,

172
00:08:56,120 --> 00:08:58,080
而是站着不动
but by standing still

173
00:08:58,190 --> 00:09:02,410
看着光线，就像它包裹着宇宙
and watching light as it wraps around the Universe.

174
00:09:02,530 --> 00:09:05,180
如果宇宙像这房间一样大
If the Universe were the size of a room

175
00:09:05,300 --> 00:09:08,920
而你拿着灯笼站在中间
and you stood in the middle of it holding up a lantern,

176
00:09:09,030 --> 00:09:11,660
光线从往向后面照射出去
light beaming out from your back

