00:09:11,770 --> 00:09:13,230
透过一扇墙
would zip out one wall

178
00:09:13,340 --> 00:09:16,130
从另一面射进来
and re-enter the room from the other side

179
00:09:16,240 --> 00:09:18,300
你会在你前面的墙
so you'd see an image of your back

180
00:09:18,410 --> 00:09:19,970
看见你后面的影像
on the wall in front of you.

181
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:22,000
看你的右边
Looking out to the right,

182
00:09:22,110 --> 00:09:25,540
你会看到光线从你的左边进来
you'd see light coming from your left side.

183
00:09:25,650 --> 00:09:28,710
这房间明显覆盖着镜子
The room would appear to be covered in mirrors.

184
00:09:28,820 --> 00:09:33,680
无论你看那扇墙，你都能看见你自己的影像
Whichever wall you looked at,you'd see an image of yourself.

185
00:09:33,790 --> 00:09:36,780
我们看星空
When we look at the night sky,

186
00:09:36,900 --> 00:09:39,220
我们看不见这种玻璃大厅
we don't see this hall of mirrors.

187
00:09:39,330 --> 00:09:41,520
空间太巨大了
But space is so vast,

188
00:09:41,630 --> 00:09:43,720
光线需要几十亿年
light could take billions of years

189
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:45,690
才能在宇宙来回一次
to loop around the Universe.

190
00:09:45,800 --> 00:09:48,930
空间和时间在这种宏大的尺度里
Space and time on this epic scale

191
00:09:49,040 --> 00:09:52,630
镜子里的影像不再一样
mean that mirror images would look nothing like one another.

192
00:09:52,740 --> 00:09:56,540
所以，想象这个畜栏是我们的宇宙
So,imagine this corral is our Universe.

193
00:09:56,650 --> 00:10:01,540
这个畜栏会被无休止的重复
There will be repeats of this corral ad infinitum,

194
00:10:01,650 --> 00:10:05,380
给我们一个生活在无限空间的错觉
giving an illusion that we live in an infinite space.

195
00:10:05,490 --> 00:10:08,310
但如果这个畜栏跨度只是30光年
But if this corral were just 30 light-years across,

196
00:10:08,430 --> 00:10:10,420
我看出去
when I look out there,

197
00:10:10,530 --> 00:10:13,050
我会看见我自己
I wouldn't see myself as I am now.

198
00:10:13,160 --> 00:10:15,150
10岁的时候
I'd see myself as a 10-year-old boy

199
00:10:15,270 --> 00:10:18,920
因为我会回看到30年前
'cause I'd be looking 30 years back in time.

200
00:10:19,040 --> 00:10:23,430
我们的银河大概存在有130亿年
Our Milky Way is around 13 billion years old.

201
00:10:23,540 --> 00:10:27,730
几乎和宇宙一样久远
It's been around almost as long as the Universe itself.

202
00:10:27,850 --> 00:10:30,140
或许有一个遥远的银河镜像
Could a distant image of the Milky Way

203
00:10:30,250 --> 00:10:32,500
躲藏在夜空里
be hidden somewhere in the night sky,

204
00:10:32,620 --> 00:10:36,980
假设你看到它5十亿或百亿年前的样子
disguised the way it looked 5 or 10 billion years ago?

205
00:10:37,090 --> 00:10:42,560
我们如何能认出它年轻时候的样子？
If it is,how would we even recognize this youthful twin?

206
00:10:46,460 --> 00:10:51,560
这些科学家相信宇宙是一个充满镜子的大厅
This scientist believes the cosmos is a hall of mirrors,

207
00:10:51,670 --> 00:10:53,860
那么宇宙是有限的
that the Universe is finite,

208
00:10:53,970 --> 00:10:57,440
而他知道它的大小和形状
and that he knows its size and shape.

209
00:11:01,540 --> 00:11:03,590
想象一下，如果整个宇宙
Imagine if the entire Universe

210
00:11:03,700 --> 00:11:06,490
就像这个房间一样大
was just the size of this room

211
00:11:07,010 --> 00:11:10,570
而空间能头尾相接的卷起来
and that space wrapped around itself

212
00:11:10,680 --> 00:11:14,440
那每扇墙都是能通过对面的通道
so each wall was the passageway to the wall opposite.

213
00:11:14,560 --> 00:11:17,680
往周围看，我会看到我自己部分的影像
Looking around,I would see myself fractured,

214
00:11:17,790 --> 00:11:21,560
就像在水晶里被多重复制
as if by a crystal,into multiple copies,

215
00:11:21,800 --> 00:11:25,050
而每个版本都能往回追溯一些
and each version would be slipped backward in time.

216
00:11:25,170 --> 00:11:27,290
往回追溯一些 追溯一些
Backward in time. Backward in time.

217
00:11:27,410 --> 00:11:30,340
是否我们的宇宙是镜子之堂
Is our Universe a hall of mirrors?

218
00:11:34,110 --> 00:11:35,360
天文学家已经用了很多年
Astronomers have looked

219
00:11:35,480 --> 00:11:37,670
去观测星系的多重结构
for repeating patterns of galaxies for years,

220
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:41,340
寻找宇宙有边的证据
looking for evidence that the Universe has an edge.

221
00:11:41,450 --> 00:11:44,050
但他们什么也没发现
But they've never found any.

222
00:11:49,490 --> 00:11:51,680
Jean-Pierre Luminet是资深科学家
Jean-Pierre Luminet is a senior scientist

223
00:11:51,790 --> 00:11:54,620
任职巴黎天文台
at the Paris Observatory.

224
00:11:54,730 --> 00:11:56,720
他从孩提时期
He's been fascinated with the shape of space

225
00:11:56,830 --> 00:11:58,850
就着迷于空间的形状
ever since he was a child.

226
00:11:58,970 --> 00:12:02,620
自然创造的形状总是很有趣
I was always interested in shapes created by nature.

227
00:12:02,740 --> 00:12:05,260
有一个很好的主意
And while it's a nice idea

228
00:12:05,370 --> 00:12:09,630
比如，去想象一种特别的，有着螺旋结构的蜗牛
to imagine a typical snail with a spiral,for instance --

229
00:12:09,740 --> 00:12:11,700
而且，你知道也有一些螺旋形星系
and you know there are spiral galaxies,for instance --

230
00:12:11,810 --> 00:12:14,600
问题是
the question is,

231
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:17,710
为什么这种形状，也会在夜空中出现
why is this shape gonna be also in the sky?

232
00:12:17,820 --> 00:12:19,240
Jean-Pierre投入极大的热情
Jean-Pierre's passion

233
00:12:19,350 --> 00:12:21,380
去探索宇宙的形状
to discover the shape of the cosmos

234
00:12:21,490 --> 00:12:23,410
这个开创性的工作源于
grew from the groundbreaking work

235
00:12:23,520 --> 00:12:25,550
阿尔伯特·爱因斯坦
of the great Albert Einstein.

236
00:12:25,660 --> 00:12:27,420
他的相对论
His theory of relativity

237
00:12:27,530 --> 00:12:30,480
显示出宇宙是一种弹性的类纤维结构
showed that space is a flexible fabric

238
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:33,990
物质和能量都会影响它
whose shape is deformed by matter and energy.

239
00:12:34,100 --> 00:12:37,730
爱因斯坦想象宇宙是一张平滑的毯
Einstein imagined the Universe as a flat sheet,

240
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:40,030
无限延伸
stretching out to infinity.

241
00:12:40,140 --> 00:12:42,460
但不表示它不能是有限的
But there's no reason it can't also be finite

242
00:12:42,580 --> 00:12:44,540
而且是头尾相接卷起来的
and curled up on itself.

243
00:12:49,420 --> 00:12:52,440
Jean-Pierre感觉他能解释这种
Jean-Pierre realized he might be able to tell the difference

244
00:12:52,550 --> 00:12:55,010
关于有限和无限宇宙之间的区别
between a finite and infinite Universe

245
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:59,780
想象宇宙是一个巨大的乐器
by thinking of the cosmos as a giant musical instrument.

246
00:12:59,890 --> 00:13:03,720
宇宙微波背景辐射
The cosmic microwave background image

247
00:13:03,830 --> 00:13:08,920
显示出宇宙在130亿年前的情况
shows us the Universe the way it was 13.7 billion years ago --

248
00:13:09,040 --> 00:13:13,790
大爆炸的余波使得炽热的流体震动
a hot liquid vibrating with aftershocks of the Big Bang,

249
00:13:13,910 --> 00:13:16,100
就像浴缸里的涟漪
like water rippling in a bathtub.

250
00:13:16,210 --> 00:13:18,100
所以，某些方面来说
So in some way,

251
00:13:18,210 --> 00:13:22,100
宇宙震动起来像钢琴或鼓
the Universe vibrated like a piano or like a drum.

252
00:13:22,220 --> 00:13:24,250
举例来说，这就是宇宙大爆炸
So,for instance,this is equivalent for the Big Bang.

253
00:13:26,490 --> 00:13:32,180
这是复杂交织的大合唱，OK？
It's a complicated mixture of many harmonics,okay?

254
00:13:32,290 --> 00:13:34,880
现在我们有基本的和声
And now we have the fundamental harmonics,

255
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:36,750
来定调
which gives the pitch.

256
00:13:36,860 --> 00:13:39,700
然后，另外一些像这样的和声
And after,the other harmonics are like this.

257
00:13:41,370 --> 00:13:42,760
再多一些
And so on,okay?

258
00:13:42,870 --> 00:13:45,930
所以，我们听到的是全局声音
So,the full sound that we can listen to

259
00:13:46,040 --> 00:13:49,630
混合了所有这些和声
is a mixture of all these harmonics.

260
00:13:49,740 --> 00:13:52,970
但你能听到的和声数量
But the number of harmonics you can hear

261
00:13:53,080 --> 00:13:55,270
取决于钢琴的大小
depends on the size of the piano.

262
00:13:55,380 --> 00:13:58,540
乐器的大小都是确定的
The size of any musical instrument is finite.

263
00:13:58,650 --> 00:14:02,910
而且比如，琴弦震动的幅度
And a string,for instance,cannot vibrate on wavelengths

264
00:14:03,020 --> 00:14:05,410
不能超过琴弦的大小
larger than the size of the string.

265
00:14:05,530 --> 00:14:07,920
所以，或许，是否我们观测的宇宙
So,maybe,if we observe that the Universe

266
00:14:08,030 --> 00:14:10,650
不能震动非常大的幅度
didn't vibrate on very long wavelengths,

267
00:14:10,760 --> 00:14:14,720
这或许可以解释，宇宙空间有着确定的大小
maybe the explanation is that space has a finite size.

268
00:14:14,840 --> 00:14:17,590
当Jean-Pierre分析这些
When Jean-Pierre analyzed the ripples

269
00:14:17,700 --> 00:14:19,830
在宇宙微波背景辐射的涟漪
in the cosmic microwave background,

270
00:14:19,940 --> 00:14:23,460
他发现最长的波纹幅度
he found that the longest wavelength ripples

271
00:14:23,580 --> 00:14:26,030
实际上，失踪了
were,indeed,missing.

272
00:14:26,150 --> 00:14:29,640
我们很惊讶，因为里面有遗失的波长
We are surprised because there was missing wavelengths,

273
00:14:29,750 --> 00:14:32,440
遗失的波动，遗失的音调
missing fluctuation,missing low tones --

274
00:14:32,550 --> 00:14:34,540
你知道，像低音
you know,like low notes.

275
00:14:34,660 --> 00:14:37,610
就像这样低，OK？
Low like this,okay?

276
00:14:37,720 --> 00:14:40,390
他们从宇宙的号叫当中迷失了
They are missing from the cosmic squall.

277
00:14:43,100 --> 00:14:45,220
Jean-Pierre对音乐的痴迷
Jean-Pierre's passion for music

278
00:14:45,330 --> 00:14:47,290
给他对于宇宙的洞察力，有深远的影响
gave him a profound cosmic insight --

279
00:14:47,400 --> 00:14:52,090
那就是宇宙是有限的
that the Universe appears to be finite.

280
00:14:52,210 --> 00:14:55,060
但，是那种形状呢？
But what shape could it be?

281
00:14:55,180 --> 00:14:57,300
Jean-Pierre花了几个月时间
Jean-Pierre spends months

282
00:14:57,410 --> 00:15:01,700
小心的测试着，这个有限宇宙不同的形状
carefully testing different shapes for his finite Universe,

283
00:15:01,820 --> 00:15:03,640
尝试让它适合宇宙微波
trying to make it fit the vibrations

284
00:15:03,750 --> 00:15:05,510
背景辐射震动的模式
of the cosmic microwave background

285
00:15:05,620 --> 00:15:07,140
精益求精的
as closely as possible,

286
00:15:07,250 --> 00:15:11,160
最后，他终于发现了…
until,finally,he finds the perfect fit...

287
00:15:14,760 --> 00:15:18,520
…一个完全相符的12面体…
...A 12-sided dodecahedron...

288
00:15:18,630 --> 00:15:20,330
一个足球
A soccer ball.

289
00:15:24,400 --> 00:15:27,500
我手里有两种类型的十二面体
Here in my hands here are two different kinds of dodechahedra.

290
00:15:27,610 --> 00:15:31,300
第一个，只是一个传统的多面体
The first one is just an ordinary dodechahedron,

291
00:15:31,410 --> 00:15:33,730
叫12个五角平面体
namely 12 pentagonal faces

292
00:15:33,850 --> 00:15:35,640
在一定程度上平均分布
arranged in a symmetrical manner.

293
00:15:35,750 --> 00:15:38,040
这是一个从远古，我们就了解的形状
This is a figure known since antiquity.

294
00:15:38,150 --> 00:15:41,440
你看到那些五角形是平面的，对吗？
You see that the Pentagons are flat,okay?

295
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:45,610
这儿有另外一个类型的球体
Here,you have a different styling of the sphere.

296
00:15:45,730 --> 00:15:48,450
你看到那些五角形是弯曲的，对吗？
You see that the Pentagons are curved,okay?

297
00:15:48,560 --> 00:15:52,090
所以这叫做圆十二面体
So this is called the circle dodecahedron.

298
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:55,120
如果Jean-Pierre是对的，那宇宙的形状
If Jean-Pierre is right,the shape of the Universe

299
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:59,190
比六边的 小行星 游戏复杂得多
is a lot more complex than a six-sided "Asteroids" game cube.

300
00:15:59,310 --> 00:16:02,160
宇宙有12边
The Universe has 12 sides,

301
00:16:02,280 --> 00:16:04,270
一面五角形
and leaving one face leads you

302
00:16:04,380 --> 00:16:07,430
对应另一面
to a matching Pentagon on the opposite side,

303
00:16:07,550 --> 00:16:09,300
但有点变形
but with a twist.

304
00:16:09,420 --> 00:16:13,340
这边的边界刚好对应另一边
This edge is exactly the same as the opposite edge.

305
00:16:13,450 --> 00:16:16,180
所以，当你到达这一点
So,as soon as you get to this point,

306
00:16:16,290 --> 00:16:19,310
你能重新进入相对的另一边空间
you re-enter your space on the opposite side,

307
00:16:19,430 --> 00:16:23,020
而且，你得转动36度
and,in addition,you have to turn by 36 degrees.

308
00:16:23,130 --> 00:16:25,550
如果宇宙是12边形
If the Universe were a dodecahedron

309
00:16:25,670 --> 00:16:27,690
只是比地球大一点点
only slightly bigger than Earth,

310
00:16:27,800 --> 00:16:30,520
光线会在一分钟环绕一圈
light would zip around it in minutes,

311
00:16:30,640 --> 00:16:33,690
你会看到地球变形的版本
and you would see twisted copies of Earth

312
00:16:33,810 --> 00:16:36,360
在天空中12个不同的方向
in a dozen different directions in the sky.

313
00:16:36,480 --> 00:16:39,630
但Jean-Pierre这种十二面体边界
But if the edges of Jean-Pierre's dodecahedron

314
00:16:39,750 --> 00:16:41,670
相隔数十亿光年
are billions of light-years apart,

315
00:16:41,780 --> 00:16:44,000
那么远的距离，和令人晕眩的倒影
the distant and faint reflections on them

316
00:16:44,120 --> 00:16:48,080
会令最细致的宇宙学家，都觉察不到
could have escaped the notice of the most careful astronomers.

317
00:16:48,190 --> 00:16:49,840
而如果这边界更远
And if the edges lie further

318
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:52,510
距离地球超过137亿光年
than 13.7 billion light-years from Earth,

319
00:16:52,630 --> 00:16:55,020
我们永远不会看到它们
we would never be able to see them

320
00:16:55,130 --> 00:16:57,280
因为我们的视线
because our view would be blocked

321
00:16:57,400 --> 00:17:01,560
被宇宙微波背景辐射的热汤阻挡了
by the hot soup of the cosmic microwave background.

322
00:17:01,670 --> 00:17:04,690
当Jean-Pierre宣布他的成果后
As soon as Jean-Pierre announced his results,

323
00:17:04,810 --> 00:17:07,660
Neil Cornish立即开始寻找
Neil Cornish begins looking for signs

324
00:17:07,770 --> 00:17:10,260
关于这个巨大足球的迹象
of his colossal soccer ball.

325
00:17:10,380 --> 00:17:11,630
他是一个NASA WMAP项目的
He's a key scientist

326
00:17:11,750 --> 00:17:14,870
主要的科学家
on a NASA spacecraft called WMAP,

327
00:17:14,980 --> 00:17:17,000
他用了5年去拍摄宇宙微波背景辐射
which spent five years photographing

328
00:17:17,120 --> 00:17:22,740
的前所未有的细节照片
the cosmic microwave background in unprecedented detail.

329
00:17:22,860 --> 00:17:25,410
然后，这是可能的宇宙模型
So,here's a possible model of the Universe

330
00:17:25,530 --> 00:17:26,910
基于12面体
based on a dodecahedron.

331
00:17:27,030 --> 00:17:29,920
里面，我们放有气球
Inside,we have a balloon

332
00:17:30,030 --> 00:17:32,190
表示可见的宇宙
representing the visible Universe,

333
00:17:32,300 --> 00:17:34,020
我们能看多远
how far we can see.

334
00:17:34,130 --> 00:17:35,360
如果是像这样
And if it was like this,

335
00:17:35,470 --> 00:17:38,030
气球在空间的位置很小
where the balloon is much smaller than the space,

336
00:17:38,140 --> 00:17:40,740
那会完全感觉不到我们生活在一个有限的宇宙
there would be no signs that we're living in a finite Universe.

337
00:17:44,080 --> 00:17:47,600
但如果可见宇宙像这样大
But if the visible Universe was so large

338
00:17:47,710 --> 00:17:51,810
那它实际上接触到12面体的边界
that it actually touched onto the edges of the dodecahedron,

339
00:17:51,920 --> 00:17:55,780
那么，光会能够缠绕穿越
then light would actually be able to travel,

340
00:17:55,890 --> 00:17:57,110
整个宇宙
wrap right around the Universe.

341
00:17:57,220 --> 00:17:59,880
所以，我们有这个适合的圆圈
So now we would have these matching circles

342
00:17:59,990 --> 00:18:01,950
在微波地带上
on the microwave sky

343
00:18:02,060 --> 00:18:07,220
这个位置上，这两个球面被阻挡，形成两个圆圈
where these two spheres intersect to form a circle.

344
00:18:07,330 --> 00:18:10,270
一个圆圈契合另一个
A circle here matching the circle down here.

345
00:18:14,240 --> 00:18:15,700
现在我们看看
Now,we have looked

346
00:18:15,810 --> 00:18:18,770
WMAP卫星收集到的宇宙微波背景辐射数据
at the microwave background data from the WMAP satellite,

347
00:18:18,880 --> 00:18:22,280
我们看不到这种圆圈契合的样式
and we haven't seen this pattern of matching circles.

348
00:18:24,620 --> 00:18:26,270
但Jean-Pierre Luminet
But Jean-Pierre Luminet

